{
  "summary": "The previous proposal correctly identifies the missing rejection reason in the web UI but conflates two distinct rejection paths: the TUI already moves rejected items from final-human-approval back to 'implementing' with feedback, while the web UI sends them to the terminal 'rejected' stage. The proposal to store human feedback as impl_review entries risks breaking automated review retry logic and can be overwritten by subsequent automated reviews. A complete fix requires: (1) the web UI must route rejections to 'implementing' not 'rejected', (2) a dedicated human_feedback field should be used instead of overloading impl_review, (3) the move API and websocket protocol need schema changes to accept a reason field, and (4) the frontend needs a text input modal for capturing rejection reasons."
